*Cut corners.** — Economizar de forma ruim.","**Money well spent.** — Dinheiro bem gasto.","**Bet on the future.** — Apostar no futuro.","**Would you rather fund science or ads?** — Você preferiria financiar ciência ou propaganda?","**I’d rather fund science.** — Prefiro financiar ciência.","**Even if results take thirty years?** — Mesmo se os resultados levarem trinta anos?"]}]},{"tag":"Verbos","title":"Verbs in focus","blocks":[{"type":"verbs","items":[{"v":"invest","pt":"investir","forms":[["I / you / we / they invest","Governments invest in science."],["he / she / it invests","Governos investem em ciência."]]}]}]},{"tag":"Escuta e diálogo","title":"Debate","blocks":[{"type":"dialog","title":"Debate","lines":[["Ana","Would you rather fund science or ads?","Você preferiria financiar ciência ou propaganda?"],["Leo","I’d rather fund science.","Prefiro financiar ciência."],["Ana","Even if results take thirty years?","Mesmo se os resultados levarem trinta anos?"],["Leo","Yes. I’d rather wait for a breakthrough.","Sim. Prefiro esperar um avanço."]]},{"type":"pron","title":"Pronúncia: Ligações e assimilação","items":[{"label":"Ligações e assimilação","note":"Sons se ligam e se transformam: did you → didja; want you → wanchu; pick it up → pi-ki-dup.","words":["did you","want you","pick it up","last night","what you"]}]}]},{"tag":"Fala","title":"Speaking","blocks":[{"type":"speak","title":"Speaking","prompts":[{"q":"State a preference.","pt":"Diga.","model":"I’d rather invest in research."},{"q":"Politely refuse.","pt":"Recuse.","model":"I’d rather not."},{"q":"Express a preference about others.","pt":"Diga.","model":"I’d rather you called me."}]}]},{"tag":"Escrita","title":"Writing","blocks":[{"type":"write","task":"Write 5 sentences with would rather about science funding or your own choices.","model":"I would rather fund research than advertising. Officials would rather see quick results. I’d rather wait for a breakthrough. I’d rather you explained the budget. Would yo